## Key Terraform Patterns

### count — multiple resources from a list
```hcl
resource "aws_subnet" "public" {
  count             = length(var.public_subnet_cidrs)
  cidr_block        = var.public_subnet_cidrs[count.index]
  availability_zone = var.availability_zones[count.index]
}
```

### dynamic block — conditional configuration block
```hcl
dynamic "route" {
  for_each = var.enable_nat_gateway ? [1] : []
  content {
    cidr_block     = "0.0.0.0/0"
    nat_gateway_id = aws_nat_gateway.this[0].id
  }
}
```

### Conditional resource creation
```hcl
resource "aws_nat_gateway" "this" {
  count = var.enable_nat_gateway ? 1 : 0
}
```

## Module Invocation

```hcl
# terraform/environments/dev/main.tf
module "vpc" {
  source = "../../modules/vpc"

  project_name         = "aws-devops"
  environment          = "dev"
  vpc_cidr             = "10.0.0.0/16"
  public_subnet_cidrs  = ["10.0.1.0/24", "10.0.2.0/24"]
  private_subnet_cidrs = ["10.0.10.0/24", "10.0.20.0/24"]
  availability_zones   = ["eu-north-1a", "eu-north-1b"]
  enable_nat_gateway   = false
}
```

## Networking Concepts

| Resource | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| VPC | Isolated virtual network — your private AWS environment |
| Public Subnet | Has route to IGW — resources reachable from internet |
| Private Subnet | No route to IGW — internal resources only |
| IGW | Internet Gateway — VPC's door to the internet |
| Route Table | Rules for where to send network traffic |
| NAT Gateway | Outbound-only internet for private subnets (~$32/month, disabled on Free Tier) |

## CIDR Planning Rules

- Leave gaps between subnet ranges for future expansion
- Private subnets: `10.0.10.x`, `10.0.20.x` — not `10.0.3.x` (leaves room for more public)
- AWS reserves 5 addresses per subnet — `/28` gives only 11 usable addresses
- `/24` = 251 usable addresses — standard for most subnets

